---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectGrid from '../components/ProjectGrid.astro';
import ProjectMedia from '../components/ProjectMedia.astro';
import Recommendation from '../components/Recommendation.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/urls';
---
<BaseLayout>
<nav class="route-rail" aria-label="Page route"><a data-route-link href="#arrival">Arrival</a><a data-route-link href="#work">Work</a><a data-route-link href="#method">Method</a><a data-route-link href="#thinking">Thinking</a><a data-route-link href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>
<section id="arrival" class="hero-section" data-element="earth" data-bearing="0"><div class="hero shell"><div><span class="route">Independent digital design & web systems</span><h1>Complexity, meet <em>clarity.</em></h1><p class="lead">Thoughtful interfaces that make the next step obvious. Explore the decisions behind better workflows, clearer identities, and more useful products.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary magnetic" href="#work">View selected work ↗</a><a class="btn" href={withBase('contact/')}>Start a project brief →</a></div><p class="privacy-copy">Three concept studies. The work, the reasoning, and the limits—openly explained.</p></div><aside class="feature-card"><div class="feature-top"><span class="route">Featured route / Atlas</span><div class="compass" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><a href={withBase('projects/atlas/')} aria-label="Explore Atlas concept case study"><ProjectMedia slug="atlas" priority alt="Atlas concept interface with four clear workflow stages"/></a><h2>Seven actions. Four decisions.</h2><p>A constructed workflow, reorganized around what needs deciding—not how many screens it has.</p><span class="badge">Concept exploration</span><a class="text-link" href={withBase('projects/atlas/#compare')}>See the transformation →</a></aside></div></section>
<section id="work" class="work-section" data-element="water" data-bearing="62"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">01 / Selected work</span><h2>See the change.<br/>Understand the choice.</h2></div><p>Three original concept studies, each showing a different way to turn an unclear experience into a useful next step. No invented clients or commercial results.</p></div><ProjectGrid/><a class="text-link" href={withBase('work/')}>Explore all work by service →</a></div></section>
<section id="method" data-element="wood" data-bearing="128"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">02 / The approach</span><h2>Discover. Shape. Deliver.</h2></div><p>A practical sequence: understand the decision, make it tangible, then check that the experience works for people.</p></div><ol class="method-grid"><li><h3>Find the real question.</h3><p>Separate the outcome someone needs from the screens, requests, and assumptions surrounding it.</p><p class="deliverable">Output / a focused problem and a decision map</p></li><li><h3>Make a choice visible.</h3><p>Compare alternative directions. Use an interface or prototype to show the tradeoff—not just describe it.</p><p class="deliverable">Output / a clear direction and an inspectable prototype</p></li><li><h3>Leave a useful system.</h3><p>Build consistent patterns, test complete journeys, and explain what has been verified and what has not.</p><p class="deliverable">Output / a working experience and an honest handoff</p></li></ol></div></section>
<section id="thinking" data-element="metal" data-bearing="218"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">03 / Find your starting point</span><h2>What are you trying to change?</h2></div><p>Choose a direction. A relevant concept and the reason it fits will appear right here.</p></div><Recommendation/></div></section>
<section data-element="earth" data-bearing="265"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">04 / From the journal</span><h2>A point of view,<br/>made practical.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={withBase('journal/')}>Read the journal →</a></div><div class="notes-grid"><article class="note-card"><span class="route">Interaction</span><h3><a href={withBase('journal/calm-can-feel-alive/')}>Calm can still feel alive.</a></h3><p>Make motion answer a question instead of becoming another question.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span class="route">Workflow</span><h3><a href={withBase('journal/decisions-not-screens/')}>Design the decision, not the screen.</a></h3><p>What the Atlas concept teaches about grouping work without hiding its complexity.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span class="route">Access</span><h3><a href={withBase('journal/reduced-motion/')}>Reduced motion is a design mode.</a></h3><p>The same meaning, without requiring the same movement.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="contact" class="next-action" data-element="fire" data-bearing="315"><div class="shell section-head"><div><span class="route">05 / A next step</span><h2>Start with what needs to change.</h2><p>A short brief is enough to make the problem concrete.</p></div><div><a class="btn primary magnetic" href={withBase('contact/')}>Prepare a project note →</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
